id=a52sxq_resolution_statusbar
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: status bar, shade header and keyguard message area follow Display > Screen resolution
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. Needs the overlay value status_bar_scale_garden_fixed_ratio = 0.8588 (proposed/overlay_framework/dimens_additions.xml) for the first item. (A) Status bar notification icons: slot width = 18dp x IndicatorScaleGardener ratio; getMaxRatio() reads IndicatorGardenPresenter.cachedGardenModel, which is half updated while a resolution switch is delivered (new status bar height, old camera top margin), so the icons were 20 % smaller at HD+ / 540p (ratio 0.75) and 9 % larger back at FHD+ (0.934) than after a boot (0.859); measured 47 / 37.5 / 36 native px. The fixed ratio takes the cached model out of the calculation. (B) Shade header battery container: SamsungBatteryViewModel.getStatusBarBatteryHeight() multiplies by the density twice (13 x density, used as sp), so at 225 dpi it fell below the 24dp header row (27 px instead of 34); the density factor is now the FHD+ constant so the row clips it at every resolution as it does at FHD+. (C) keyguard_message_area_container and the auth message area in it take their top margins (status bar height, 20dp) once when the shade window is inflated; after a live switch the lock screen / bouncer message text sat 1.5x / 2x too low. The margin update AOSP does on configuration changes is restored.
